claimed: okay-script-web -- the remaining half of "a new JSP" (request-object injection, filed in BACKLOG after okay-script-page). Scoped to avoid the dependency concern the backlog entry itself named: a plain, dependency-free okay.script.Web(method, path, query, headers) value plus Web.current/setCurrent (the same proven always-fresh-method pattern as Meta.current, NOT a given), with NO okay.http.Request import in okay-script's own code -- a caller (an okay-jetty route) translates its own real Request into Web before calling render(). Page.render(web: Web = Web.current) sets it atomically inside the page's existing lock, so concurrent requests to the SAME Page do not race on which request's Web value a given render() call sees. ScalaScript.render gets the same optional web param for API symmetry, with the same single-threaded caveat Meta.current already documents for the un-synchronized one-shot path.
